# Learn & Play's functions translated without per-access fences (tools/ws7/recomp/xlat/relaxed.py says why and how), by
# address: names/relaxed.list has the Mac's kernels, which aren't all matched here. These are the hottest functions of the
# Wwise thread (0x1a823c0) and the note detection in a song (Time Profiler, 2026-11-06). Each was read for what relaxed.py
# asks: a loop counted over buffers or the effect's own state, no write to a global, no wait on memory, no lock prefix.
# 0x1a35660, 0x1a35ba0 and 0x1a08300 are as hot but set a static's guard (0x1ed2598), so they stay fenced.
0x1a03d60   Wwise: SSE filter over a buffer (prefetchnta, counted loops)
0x1a05bf0   Wwise: delay line and SSE mix over a buffer
0x1a0ab70   Wwise: scalar SSE resampler loop
0x1a17d30   Wwise: SSE effect over a buffer, parameters from its own object
0x1a0c7b0   Wwise: SSE kernel of 0x1a0d120
0x1a0d120   Wwise: SSE mix over channels, calls 0x1a0c7b0
0x1a34ae0   Wwise: counted mix of two buffers
0x1a3ccd0   Wwise: SSE delay network
0x1a3d420   Wwise: SSE delay network, the Mac's roomverb_fdn by shape, not proved
0x1a3e3e0   Wwise: counted loops over a delay line
0x1a8fa60   Wwise: counted copy with gain
0x1aaade0   Wwise: inner loop of 0x1aaaf00
0x1aaaf00   Wwise: SSE transform with a fixed table, calls 0x1aaade0
0x1ab4100   Wwise: x87 filter over a buffer
0x10622d0   note detection: x87 scan of a spectrum, counted
0x13f23e0   note detection: SSE FFT pass
0x13f2d50   note detection: bit reversal and packing of the FFT's data
